.EE

.PP
Verify a slug or ID against organizations available to the saved OAuth
session, then store its slug as the active organization.

.PP
--org and AXILIO_ORG override this stored selection. API keys remain
bound to their own organization and cannot use this command.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API-key auth cannot switch orgs; use a saved
OAuth session
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the membership check; overrides
AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - No effect on orgs use command; its confirmation is
unstyled
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Does not choose the org to save; the positional
slug or ID does
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON
active-organization result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the human org-selection confirmation;
JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio orgs list
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
   SLUG         NAME          ID
*  example-org  Example Inc.  <organization-id>
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio orgs use example-org
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.EX
Active organization set to example-org (Example Inc.).
.EE

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.SH phone
.EX
axilio phone
.EE

.PP
Running \fBaxilio phone\fR without a subcommand is equivalent to \fBaxilio
phone --help\fR: it only displays this help and does not observe or
control a phone. Phone and global flags shown here therefore have no
effect. Pass flags to a phone subcommand instead.

.PP
Drive a phone leased with \fBaxilio sessions start\fR\&.

.PP
A reliable loop is observe the screen, find or semantically target an
element, act, then observe again to verify.

.PP
Available verbs are observe, find, find-text, tap, long-press, swipe,
type, key, screenshot, wait-for, and send. Every successful verb emits a
structured result with -o json.

.PP
Session selection precedence is --session, AXILIO_SESSION, the sole
active local lease, the saved current-session pointer, then an ambiguity
error. The verbs mirror the SDK MobileDriver so an explored interaction
maps directly onto SDK code.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on phone command; bare axilio phone
only displays this help

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on phone command; bare axilio phone
only displays this help
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on phone command; bare axilio phone
only displays this help
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - No effect on phone command; bare axilio phone only
displays this help
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on phone command; bare axilio phone only
displays this help
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on phone command; bare axilio
phone only displays this help (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - No effect on phone command; bare axilio phone
only displays this help

.PP
\fBWorkflow examples\fP

.EX
axilio phone observe
axilio phone tap --query "the search box"
axilio phone type "Axilio"
axilio phone observe
.EE

.SS find
.EX
axilio phone find <query> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Locate one visible element from a natural-language description and
return its text, center, bounding box, confidence, and source.

.PP
The OCR engine defaults to free, the vision model is selected by the
server, and the effective deadline is 10 seconds when --timeout is
omitted. A missing target is an error; use \fBfind-text\fR for a successful
empty result.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--model\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Vision model override; omitted lets the server
select the model
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--ocr-engine\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OCR engine: free or premium; omitted uses
free
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--timeout\fP=\fIduration\fP - Vision deadline such as 15s; omitted uses
10s (default "0s")

.PP
\fBParent options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Session ID; overrides AXILIO_SESSION,
sole-lease, and current-pointer selection

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect; the session's embedded control
token in the websocket URL authenticates phone commands
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on phone find command; it does not
call the Axilio API
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
found-element result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on phone find command; phone control is
selected by session, not org
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the found-element result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for vision search; the
found-element result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone find "the search box"
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
Text        Search
Center      540,620
BBox        80,560 920x120
Confidence  0.99
Source      ocr
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone find "settings icon" --ocr-engine premium
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
Text
Center      900,120
BBox        840,60 120x120
Confidence  0.98
Source      vlm
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP Vision-model elements can have no text; coordinates depend on the
current frame.

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone find "continue button" --timeout 15s -o json
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
{
  "text": "Continue",
  "center": {"x": 540, "y": 1120},
  "bbox": {"x": 80, "y": 1060, "width": 920, "height": 120},
  "confidence": 0.98,
  "source": "ocr"
}
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP Element content and coordinates depend on the current frame.

.SS find-text
.EX
axilio phone find-text <text> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Search OCR text without semantic vision.

.PP
By default, match a case-insensitive substring and return the first
element. --exact uses a case-sensitive exact match. No match is
successful: table output prints \fBNo match.\fR and JSON output is null
rather than a not-found error.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--exact\fP - Require a case-sensitive exact match instead of
case-insensitive substring

.PP
\fBParent options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Session ID; overrides AXILIO_SESSION,
sole-lease, and current-pointer selection

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect; the session's embedded control
token in the websocket URL authenticates phone commands
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on phone find-text command; it does
not call the Axilio API
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
text-match result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on phone find-text command; phone
control is selected by session, not org
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the text-match result as table
or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for OCR search; the
text-match result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone find-text "sign in"
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
Text        Sign in
Center      540,1120
BBox        80,1060 920x120
Confidence  0.98
Source      ocr
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP The default is a case-insensitive substring match.

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone find-text "Sign in" --exact
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
Text        Sign in
Center      540,1120
BBox        80,1060 920x120
Confidence  0.98
Source      ocr
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP Exact matching is case-sensitive.

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone find-text "settings"
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
No match.
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP No match is success; -o json emits null.

.PP
\fBSample 4\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone find-text "settings" -o json
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
null
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP No match is a successful literal JSON null.

.SS key
.EX
axilio phone key <name>
.EE

.PP
Press a named key on the selected phone.

.PP
The only named key currently supported by the CLI and pinned mobile
driver is \fBenter\fR; back, home, and other key names are not available.

.PP
\fBParent options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Session ID; overrides AXILIO_SESSION,
sole-lease, and current-pointer selection

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect; the session's embedded control
token in the websocket URL authenticates phone commands
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on phone key command; it does not
call the Axilio API
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - No effect on phone key command; its runtime message
is unstyled
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on phone key command; the target is
selected by session, not org
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON key
press result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the human key press result; the phone
action still runs; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone key enter
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.EX
Pressed enter
.EE

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.SS long-press
.EX
axilio phone long-press <x> <y> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Press and hold at frame-space pixel coordinates, with (0,0) at the
screen's top-left.

.PP
This command is coordinate-only; use observe or find to inspect the
current frame before choosing a point. The default hold duration is 800
milliseconds.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--duration-ms\fP=\fInumber\fP - How long to hold the coordinate, in
milliseconds (default "800")

.PP
\fBParent options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Session ID; overrides AXILIO_SESSION,
sole-lease, and current-pointer selection

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect; the session's embedded control
token in the websocket URL authenticates phone commands
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on phone long-press command; it
does not call the Axilio API
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - No effect on phone long-press command; its runtime
message is unstyled
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on phone long-press command; the target
is selected by session, not org
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON
long-press result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the human long-press result; the phone
action still runs; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone long-press 540 1080
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.EX
Long-pressed 540,1080 for 800ms
.EE

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone long-press 540 1080 --duration-ms 1200
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.EX
Long-pressed 540,1080 for 1200ms
.EE

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.SS observe
.EX
axilio phone observe [flags]
.EE

.PP
Capture and analyze the selected phone's current screen.

.PP
OCR uses the free engine when --ocr-engine is omitted. Table output
lists recognized text with center coordinates and confidence, then
summarizes icons and screen dimensions. JSON returns the complete screen
object, including texts, icons, dimensions, screen hash, and capture
time.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--ocr-engine\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OCR engine: free or premium; omitted uses
free

.PP
\fBParent options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Session ID; overrides AXILIO_SESSION,
sole-lease, and current-pointer selection

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect; the session's embedded control
token in the websocket URL authenticates phone commands
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on phone observe command; it does
not call the Axilio API
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
observation result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on phone observe command; phone control
is selected by session, not org
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the observation result as table
or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for observation; the
observation result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone observe
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
TEXT          X    Y     CONF
coffee shops  540  620   0.99
Continue      540  1120  0.98
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.EX
2 texts, 0 icons  1080x2400
.EE

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP JSON includes texts, icons, dimensions, screen hash, and capture time.

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone observe --ocr-engine premium
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
TEXT          X    Y     CONF
coffee shops  540  620   0.99
Continue      540  1120  0.98
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.EX
2 texts, 0 icons  1080x2400
.EE

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP Premium OCR changes recognition, not the table shape.

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone observe -o json
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
{
  "texts": [
    {"text": "Continue", "center": {"x": 540, "y": 1120}, "confidence": 0.98}
  ],
  "icons": [],
  "hash": "<screen-hash>",
  "width": 1080,
  "height": 2400,
  "captured_at": "<timestamp>"
}
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP Shortened representative screen JSON; elements also include bounding
boxes and sources.

.PP
\fBWalkthrough\fP

.EX
+----------------------------+
| Search                     |
| [ coffee shops           ] |  text "coffee shops"  540,620  0.99
|                            |
| [        Continue        ] |  text "Continue"     540,1120  0.98
+----------------------------+
right-side fields: text, center (x,y), confidence
frame 1080x2400; frame-space pixels; (0,0) is top-left

reuse the observed Continue center:
axilio phone tap 540 1120
.EE

.SS screenshot
.EX
axilio phone screenshot [flags]
.EE

.PP
Capture the selected phone's screen as PNG bytes and write them to
--out.

.PP
The default destination is screenshot.png in the current directory. If
the destination already exists, its contents are overwritten without
confirmation; the CLI does not create a backup. On success the human
result reports the path and byte count.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--out\fP=\fIvalue\fP - PNG path to create; overwrite existing contents
without confirmation (default "screenshot.png")

.PP
\fBParent options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Session ID; overrides AXILIO_SESSION,
sole-lease, and current-pointer selection

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect; the session's embedded control
token in the websocket URL authenticates phone commands
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on phone screenshot command; it
does not call the Axilio API
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - No effect on phone screenshot command; its runtime
message is unstyled
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on phone screenshot command; the target
is selected by session, not org
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON
screenshot write result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the human screenshot result; the phone
action still runs; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone screenshot
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.EX
Wrote screenshot.png (<bytes> bytes)
.EE

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP A new file requests mode 0644, subject to the process umask. Overwriting
an existing file preserves its mode while replacing its contents.

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone screenshot --out login.png
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.EX
Wrote login.png (<bytes> bytes)
.EE

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP A new file requests mode 0644, subject to the process umask. Overwriting
an existing file preserves its mode while replacing its contents.

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone screenshot --out ./login.png
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.EX
Wrote ./login.png (<bytes> bytes)
.EE

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP Deliberate correction of the legacy artifacts/login.png example:
screenshot does not create missing parent directories, so this target
uses the existing current directory. A new file requests mode 0644
subject to umask; overwrite preserves the existing mode.

.SS send
.EX
axilio phone send <path> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Upload a local file into the org library and push it into the phone's
media library so it appears in the gallery.

.PP
Targets the current session's phone (override with --session). Supported
images are jpg, jpeg, png, webp, gif, and heic; supported videos are
mp4, webm, mov, 3gp, and mkv. The target collection is inferred by media
type unless DCIM, Pictures, or Movies is selected. Phones accept
deliveries up to 100 MiB. By default the command returns after dispatch;
--wait blocks for delivered or failed, and --timeout applies only with
--wait. This combines \fBuploads add\fR and \fBuploads push\fR and therefore
retains the upload in the org library.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--collection\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Target DCIM, Pictures, or Movies; omitted
infers from media type
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--timeout\fP=\fIduration\fP - Maximum delivery wait; applies only with
--wait (default "1m0s")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--wait\fP - Block until the phone reports delivered or failed instead
of returning at dispatch

.PP
\fBParent options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Session ID; overrides AXILIO_SESSION,
sole-lease, and current-pointer selection

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the upload-and-delivery request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the upload-and-delivery request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
delivery result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the upload-and-delivery request;
overrides AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the delivery result as table or
json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress upload progress and delivery notes; the
delivery result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone send ./photo.jpg
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
Delivery  <delivery-id>
File      photo.jpg
Status    dispatched
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.EX
→ Sending photo.jpg to phone <phone-id>
pushed; re-run with --wait to confirm delivery
.EE

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP The upload remains in the organization library.

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone send ./clip.mp4 --collection Movies
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
Delivery  <delivery-id>
File      clip.mp4
Status    dispatched
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.EX
→ Sending clip.mp4 to phone <phone-id>
pushed; re-run with --wait to confirm delivery
.EE

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP The upload remains in the organization library and is delivered to
Movies.

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio phone send ./photo.jpg --wait --timeout 2m
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
Delivery  <delivery-id>
File      photo.jpg
Status    delivered
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.EX
→ Sending photo.jpg to phone <phone-id>
.EE

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP With --wait, the command returns only after delivered, failed, or the
two-minute deadline.

.SS swipe
.EX
axilio phone swipe <x1> <y1> <x2> <y2> [flags]
.EE

.PP
