.SH sessions
.EX
axilio sessions
.EE

.PP
Running \fBaxilio sessions\fR without a subcommand is equivalent to \fBaxilio
sessions --help\fR: it only displays this help and does not acquire, list,
select, or stop sessions. Global flags shown here therefore have no
effect. Pass flags to a sessions subcommand instead.

.PP
Manage the phone leases used by \fBaxilio phone\fR\&. Starting a session
stores a local lease file and a current-session pointer until the
session is stopped. Session selection precedence is --session,
AXILIO_SESSION, the sole active lease, the current-session pointer, then
an ambiguity error. \fBsessions list --remote\fR instead asks the API for
all active server sessions.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on sessions command; bare axilio
sessions only displays this help
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on sessions command; bare axilio
sessions only displays this help
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - No effect on sessions command; bare axilio sessions
only displays this help
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on sessions command; bare axilio
sessions only displays this help
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on sessions command; bare
axilio sessions only displays this help (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - No effect on sessions command; bare axilio
sessions only displays this help

.PP
\fBWorkflow examples\fP

.EX
axilio sessions start
axilio sessions list
axilio sessions current
axilio sessions stop sess_123
axilio sessions stop <session-id>
.EE

.SS current
.EX
axilio sessions current
.EE

.PP
Resolve and show the session selected for phone commands.

.PP
Phone command session selection precedence is --session, AXILIO_SESSION,
the sole active local lease, the saved current-session pointer, then an
ambiguity error. This command has no --session flag, so it starts at
AXILIO_SESSION. If no session resolves, the current implementation
prints a note and exits successfully.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on sessions current command; it uses
local session data or its control URL
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on sessions current command; it
does not call the Axilio API
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
current-session result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on sessions current command; phone
control is selected by session, not org
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the current-session result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for session resolution;
the current-session result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio sessions current
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
Session  <session-id>
Phone    <phone-id>
Type     android
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP No selected session is an exit-0 answer; JSON prints null.

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
AXILIO_SESSION=sess_123 axilio sessions current
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
Session  sess_123
Phone    <phone-id>
Type     android
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP The named lease must exist locally; AXILIO_SESSION has precedence over
sole-lease and current-pointer selection.

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio sessions current -o json
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
{
  "session_id": "<session-id>",
  "phone_id": "<phone-id>",
  "phone_type": "android",
  "control_url": "<control-url>",
  "created_at": "<timestamp>"
}
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP With no selected lease, the successful JSON result is null.

.SS list
.EX
axilio sessions list [flags]
.EE

.PP
List local lease files by default.

.PP
The \fB*\fR marker identifies the lease that phone commands would select in
this shell when resolution is not ambiguous. Use --remote to list active
server sessions instead; remote rows include session ID, phone ID, phone
type, and model but are not the local lease registry.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--remote\fP - List all active server sessions instead of this CLI's
local lease files

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Authenticates only --remote listing; no effect
on local lease files
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Selects the API host only with --remote; no
effect on local lease files
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable session
listing
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Selects the OAuth org only with --remote; no
effect on local lease files
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render local or remote sessions as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes; the session listing
remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio sessions list
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
   SESSION       PHONE       TYPE
*  <session-id>  <phone-id>  android
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP With no local leases, stdout says how to acquire one and exit status is
0.

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio sessions list --remote
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
SESSION       PHONE       TYPE     MODEL
<session-id>  <phone-id>  android  Pixel 8
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP Remote results come from the API and do not mark the locally selected
lease.

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio sessions list -o json
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
[
  {
    "session_id": "<session-id>",
    "phone_id": "<phone-id>",
    "phone_type": "android",
    "control_url": "<control-url>",
    "created_at": "<timestamp>"
  }
]
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP Local lease JSON includes the stored control URL; IDs and URLs vary.

.SS start
.EX
axilio sessions start [flags]
.EE

.PP
Acquire an Android phone by default and persist its session as a local
lease and current-session pointer.

.PP
Select iphone with --phone-type, pin a dedicated phone discovered
through \fBphones mine\fR with --phone-id, or attach the session to a
workflow with --workflow. --export prints only \fBexport
AXILIO_SESSION=\\<id\\>\fR for shell eval; that shell syntax also wins when
-o json is supplied. The lease remains active until explicitly stopped.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--export\fP - Print only \fBexport AXILIO_SESSION=\\<id\\>\fR for shell
eval
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--phone-id\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Pin a dedicated phone ID from \fBphones mine\fR
instead of pool allocation
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--phone-type\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Phone platform to allocate: android or
iphone (default "android")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--workflow\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Workflow ID to attach; omit for an
interactive lease

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the phone-allocation request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the phone-allocation request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
allocated-session result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the phone-allocation request;
overrides AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the allocated session as table
or json; --export always emits shell text (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress session guidance; the result or
--export text remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio sessions start
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
Session      <session-id>
Phone        <phone-id>
Region       us-central
Live view    <live-view-url>
Control URL  <control-url>
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.EX
Drive it:  axilio phone observe
Pin it to this shell (for parallel work):  export AXILIO_SESSION=<session-id>
Release it with:  axilio sessions stop <session-id>
.EE

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio sessions start --phone-type iphone
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
Session      <session-id>
Phone        <phone-id>
Region       us-central
Live view    <live-view-url>
Control URL  <control-url>
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.EX
Drive it:  axilio phone observe
Pin it to this shell (for parallel work):  export AXILIO_SESSION=<session-id>
Release it with:  axilio sessions stop <session-id>
.EE

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio sessions start --phone-id ph_123
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
Session      <session-id>
Phone        ph_123
Region       us-central
Live view    <live-view-url>
Control URL  <control-url>
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.EX
Drive it:  axilio phone observe
Pin it to this shell (for parallel work):  export AXILIO_SESSION=<session-id>
Release it with:  axilio sessions stop <session-id>
.EE

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBSample 4\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio sessions start --workflow wf_123
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
Session      <session-id>
Phone        <phone-id>
Region       us-central
Live view    <live-view-url>
Control URL  <control-url>
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.EX
Drive it:  axilio phone observe
Pin it to this shell (for parallel work):  export AXILIO_SESSION=<session-id>
Release it with:  axilio sessions stop <session-id>
.EE

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBSample 5\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
axilio sessions start --export
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.EX
export AXILIO_SESSION=<session-id>
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP --export emits shell text even when -o json is also supplied.

.PP
\fBSample 6\fP

.PP
\fBInvocation\fP

.EX
eval "$(axilio sessions start --export)"
.EE

.PP
\fBStandard output\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBStandard error\fP

.PP
None.

.PP
\fBExit status:\fP 0.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP The shell consumes the nested command's export line and sets
